.TH TTS_TEMPLATES.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
tts_templates.yaml \- spoken\-text templates for Big Red Box alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/tts_templates.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
A YAML mapping from
.B system_id
patterns to the sentence that
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1)
speaks when it accepts an alert.
It is read once at startup from
.BR DAQ_ALERT_TTS_TEMPLATE_FILE ,
default
.IR config/tts_templates.yaml ,
resolved relative to the listener's current directory.
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1)
changes to the checkout first, so there it resolves to the shipped file.
.PP
Keys are
.BR fnmatch (3)\-style
glob patterns
.RB ( * ,
.BR ? ,
.BR [...] )
matched against the alert's
.BR system_id ,
in file order; the first match wins.
Matching is case\-sensitive on Linux and macOS and case\-insensitive on
Windows (Python
.B fnmatch.fnmatch
normalises case with
.BR os.path.normcase ).
The key
.B default
is used when no pattern matches.
.PP
Values are Python
.B str.format
templates with three fields:
.TP
.B {system_id}
.TP
.B {timestamp}
the sender's timestamp string, verbatim
.TP
.B {message}
.PP
A missing payload field is rendered as
.BR UNKNOWN ,
or
.B (no message text)
for
.BR message .
.SH FALLBACKS
The built\-in template
.B "Critical error on {system_id}. {message}"
is used when:
.IP \(bu 2
the file does not exist (silently, with no log line);
.IP \(bu 2
the file cannot be read, does not parse, or is not a mapping (a warning is
logged);
.IP \(bu 2
no pattern matches and there is no
.B default
key;
.IP \(bu 2
the chosen template names an unknown field or is malformed (a warning is
logged and the built\-in template is used for that alert).
.PP
Entries whose key or value is not a string are skipped with a warning.
The templates are shared by both speech backends
.RB ( qt " and " aws ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/tts_templates.yaml
The shipped file, with patterns for
.BR Run\-Contr* ,
.BR *Crash* ,
.BR DAQ\-NODE\-* ,
.B CFO*
and
.BR ROC* .
It is not included in the Python wheel.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_TEMPLATE_FILE
Path of the template file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
default: "Critical error on {system_id}. {message}"
"Run\-Contr*": "Run Control Error.  {message}"
"DAQ\-NODE\-*": "Attention. Node {system_id} reports a critical error. {message}"
"CFO*": "C. F. O. {system_id} has a critical error. {message}"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quote keys that start with
.B *
or contain
.BR : ;
an unquoted leading
.B *
is a YAML alias.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
